\section{Nodes}{

Node area is proportional to the sample size (\code{node_size = "n"}), or to
the number of studies (\code{"studies"}), or equal. \code{node_size_range} gives the
smallest and largest radius in layout units (the network spans about -1 to
1). \code{node_fill} is one colour, one colour per treatment, or \code{"auto"} with
\code{palette} (any \code{\link[grDevices:hcl.colors]{grDevices::hcl.colors()}} palette name). The reference
treatment is filled with \code{reference_fill} (grey); \code{highlight} recolours
chosen treatments with \code{highlight_color}.
}

\section{Edges}{

Width follows the number of direct studies (\code{edge_width = "studies"})
within \code{edge_width_range} (mm); edges are black (\code{edge_color}). The count
is printed in a white circle with a black border on each edge
(\code{edge_labels}, \code{edge_label_size}); \code{edge_label_fill = NA} prints plain
numbers nudged off the line instead. \code{edge_style = "multi"} draws one thin line
per study; \code{min_studies} hides comparisons with fewer studies.
\code{multiarm = TRUE} shades the polygon of each multi-arm trial.
}

\section{Labels}{

Treatment names are bold with \verb{n = ... (x\% of total)} underneath, the
share being that treatment's participants over all arms (\code{show_n = FALSE}
drops the line). Names longer than \code{label_wrap} characters
are wrapped. \code{labels} supplies display names (a named vector is safest).
Labels sit outside the node, every row centred; \code{label_offset} moves them
further out. \code{label_box = TRUE} draws a white container behind each label,
and a colour (\code{label_box = "#F3F4F6"}) fills the container with it.
}

\section{Legend and titles}{

The legend (\code{legend = TRUE} by default) is one framed box under the
network with sections for node size, the circled study count on the
edges and, when a ring is drawn, the ring groups. \code{title} defaults to "Network of Interventions",
centred (\code{title_align = "left"} for the other style); \code{outcome} becomes
the subtitle; \code{caption} is printed in italics at the bottom right.
\code{font_family = "serif"} gives the reference look, \code{"sans"} a plainer one.
\code{grid = TRUE} adds a light background grid; \code{background} sets the page
colour (pair it with \code{label_color} and \code{title_color} for dark themes).
}

